.TH tapectl-tenant-add 1  "tapectl-tenant-add " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-tenant\-add \- Add a new tenant (mints a primary and a backup key pair, or adopts an existing identity with \-\-adopt\-key)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl tenant add\fR [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-description\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-adopt\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add a new tenant (mints a primary and a backup key pair, or adopts an existing identity with \-\-adopt\-key)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
Description
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-adopt\-key\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Adopt this existing age identity file (the SECRET: one AGE\-SECRET\-KEY\-1… line; age\-keygen\*(Aqs comment lines are kept) as the tenant\*(Aqs primary key instead of minting a pair. It is stored byte for byte as keys/<name>\-primary.age.key, mode 0600, and is the tenant\*(Aqs only key: nothing is minted. Refused: anything but one X25519 identity, a public key already registered, and the escrow identity\*(Aqs secret
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
No live progress on stderr. Long operations (stage create, volume write/resume/verify/read\-slices, restore) still write their session log under <home>/logs/
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, stage reports. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home.
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, stage\-reports, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Tenant name
